<title>GERMANY: Germany approves Rheinmetall's STN buy.</title>
<headline>Germany approves Rheinmetall's STN buy.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>German cartel authorities have approved the purchase of defence electronics maker STN Atlas Elektronik GmbH by a group including Rheinmetall AG, Badenwerk AG and British Aerospace plc, Rheinmetall said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The purchase of STN Atlas, formerly part of Bremer Vulkan, is part of a broad consolidation in the German defence industry. European cartel authorities had passed the decision to the Berlin office in April.  </p>
<p>Rheinmetall intends to merge the engines and aerial defence systems into a new company, Elektronische Fahrzeugsysteme GmbH, in which competitors Kkrauss Maffei and Wegmann will each hold 25 percent.</p>
<p>EFS will have annual sales of 120 million marks ($68.2 million) and employ 150 workers.</p>
<p>-- Terence Gallagher, Bonn newsroom, 49-228-2609750</p>
<p>($ = 1.759 German Marks)</p>
</text>
